## Rules

1. Change ONLY the sentence or paragraph that each issue points at. Leave every other sentence, paragraph, heading, punctuation mark, and line break byte-for-byte unchanged.
2. When the issue is an unsourced or contradicted number, remove the number or replace it with qualitative wording (for example 「点击率高 30%」 becomes 「点击率表现良好」).
3. Introduce NO new numbers, statistics, dates, percentages, or monetary figures.
4. Introduce NO new claims. Do not add analysis, opinions, or filler.
5. When the issue is an unverifiable absolutism, hunt down every outcome-promise token (搞定、学会、包会、速成、保证、决定、必然、一定、满分、精通、逆袭、躺赢) in the flagged sentence and its heading, and replace each with a hedged, checkable statement of the same intent (「让你周报满分」 becomes 「帮你在周报上少走弯路」; 「3步搞定」 becomes 「3步走下来，周报会顺很多」). A rewrite that still contains any of these tokens in the flagged sentence is NOT a fix.
6. Preserve the original language, tone, and formatting.

## Output Format

Return a JSON object with these exact keys:

{
  "rewritten_content": "string — the FULL rewritten content, with only the flagged sentences/paragraphs changed",
  "notes": [
    "string — one short line per change you made, naming the sentence you edited"
  ]
}

The `rewritten_content` field must contain the complete content, not a fragment.
